[1] Array Processing vs Vector processing <mumbo jumbo>

-- Core idea is that of Pipelines and Parallel Pipelines:
 ----- Pipelines ------
  If your instructions are Vector Instructions (meaning the operate on Vector Registers)
  -- then individual lane operations are independent (no control flow)
  -- thus functional units (like ALU, LSU) can be deeply pipelined
     -- aka `n' lanes can be loaded into a functional unit from SIMD-n in one shot
     	-- in different stages of their pipeline (AKA Perfect Pipelining)
 ----- Parallel Pipelines ------
  -- On top of that, if you want to give your functional Units width then do so
     -- ALUx4 can operate on SIMD-64 by loading SIMD16 on each ALU and have 4 of these operate at the same time
     -- Same story with the LSU

  -- Also since these instructions are loaded meaning a VMUL64 is a like a for loop of 64 SMUL instructions
    -- So this helps reduce Instruct fetch, decode and schedule
    -- aka your trip through the Front End is going to be shorter
    
