[5] Memory Banking : This is where his slides start to pick up
  -- Consider a VEC LSU
  -- If the underlying SRAM has `n' banks and they all share the same ADDR and DATA bus
    -- then only 1 bank can load ADDR on a cycle and 1 bank can store DATA on a cycle

  -- So to get VEC64 LOAD fully pipelined for a 16-cycle bank access latency, you want a LOAD64 to issue
     16 x 4 of these into the LSU
     -- If you can find 16 of them at a time that go to 16 different banks then you can fully hide the access latency
     -- Of course LSU should respect VMASK

